Title: F2-M01 — A Line in the Snow (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

> FADE IN:

INT. MOUNTAIN OPERATIONS ROOM - DAWN

[[AMBIENCE: radio hiss, distant engines, wind against canvas]]
[[MUSIC: restrained military tension]]

A map of the operational area is spread across a table. COMMANDER SAVA and PETROV stand over it. Sava has an old field compass in one hand.

COMMANDER SAVA
(serious)
Command says the Compact struck first and the junction was abandoned in haste. Whoever left it did not leave in a hurry; the stoves were cold.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: junction on the north road, player yard and refinery south of it, raider outpost with four structures north, east road marked as relief approach, old service tunnel north-west unmarked]]

PETROV
(measured)
Tracks lead north, but the snow has hidden their numbers.

PETROV
Outpost is four structures on the north road, light guard. Two hundred metres from our yard, and the east road is open behind us.

COMMANDER SAVA
(clipped)
The risk is the column. We have six riflemen, one harvester, and no reserve if the yard burns. Power and a barracks first. Nothing moves north before that.

PETROV
Fuel depots in the outpost. If we stand close when they go, we go with them.

COMMANDER SAVA
(firm)
Establish a foothold and clear the junction. Expect a second group to emerge once we commit.

COMMANDER SAVA
(quieter)
And Petrov — anything they leave behind, I want it bagged before it goes in a report. Not after.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

> FADE OUT.
